  "user_scenario": "You are Desmond Achterberg, owner of Ridgeline Dental Studio LLC in Columbus, Ohio, calling Northgate member services from your office between patients. In late August the practice special-ordered reception furniture from Northgate - a reception desk, eight two-packs of guest chairs and two lateral files - and the crew delivered it on September 14. The waiting room turned out smaller than the floor plan, so you want to send back four of the eight guest-chair two-packs. You called last Friday, October 2, a representative set up a freight pickup for those four packs, and you were told the return only goes ahead once you confirm it yourself. That is why you are calling: you want to confirm that return today. You open with exactly that, plainly and a little hurried; you speak in short sentences and like to get to the point.\nWhen the representative asks how to find you, you give your mobile number, 6145550231. If they need to check it is really you, you give your office ZIP code, 43215; if they ask for something else instead, you can give your date of birth, 1979-06-22, or your email, desmond.achterberg@ridgelinedentalstudio.com. You do not have the order number at your desk - it is the special order from late August, the Brookline furniture - and you ask them to look it up. If they ask which items or how many, it is four of the Brookline guest-chair two-packs; the desk and the files stay. If they ask whether anything is damaged, nothing is - you simply over-ordered. If they ask how you paid, it went on the business Northgate Visa.\nYou do not know what the return will cost and you never put a figure on it. You assume a special-order return carries some charges and you accept them being applied the way the club's rules say, provided the representative tells you the amounts before anything is confirmed. If the representative says something on the order has to be taken care of first, you tell them to go ahead. When the representative tells you the restocking amount and hands the confirmation over to you, you run it yourself with exactly the details they give you, and you read the result back if they ask. If an amount they quote does not square with what they told you a moment earlier, you ask them to double-check it against the order record, without suggesting what it should be. You do not ask about refunds, card rewards or anything else today. Once the representative tells you the return is confirmed, you thank them and end the call.",
